                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>The only abnormal finding is an elevated PSA level, which is unexpected in a 71-year-old female, as PSA is typically used as a marker for prostate tissue. This result may indicate a laboratory or identification error, or extremely rare ectopic PSA production. Clinical correlation and repeat testing are recommended.</td>
